# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of
# platform or a developer's global `core.autocrlf` setting. A CRLF-
# terminated shebang line fails to exec on Linux ("no such file or
# directory") - these scripts run as Docker image entrypoints/CMDs, so a
# corrupted checkout breaks every container built from it, not just local
# tooling. See RP-08 in docs/devdocs/runtime-platform/README.md in the
# parent website-control-panel repo.
*.sh text eol=lf
